s of growth to invest in but that  growth is slowed or even stopped for  netflix they are rethinking a lot of  projects moving forwards but the  alienation project would be a reasonably  low budget thing it's a very high  concept series it has lots of social  commentary it has lots of different ways  you can do what sci-fi does best and  actually have layers to it and talk  about lots of different real life issues  through the metaphor alva alien cop  buddy series and if the series has the  same humor and joy that the movie did in  the following series did then there's no  reason why this couldn't be a massive  success  but there are lots of other projects  stuck in developmental that could do the  same for example for years now they've  been trying to do an 18 movie a sequel  to the movie a few years ago that kind  of bombed now i really hoped when liam  neeson stepped up to take on the moniker  of hannibal that that would lead to a  series of movies i thought it was a  brilliant idea i thought bradley cooper  as faceman was just genius casting and i  really hoped we would get two three four  movies out of it but it never happened  mainly because the movie just wasn't  that popular at the box office the  reason though for me was again this is a  character-driven project you need to  care about hannibal face mad murdoc and  ba and if you don't if you're not  invested in them it doesn't work  so again this is a project forget about  trying to make a movie you should be  making a streaming service series  knight rider has been in pre-production  for a few years now james 1 has got 31  projects currently on his imdb list of  upcoming from arachnophobia to mortal  kombat 2 to oh god the list just goes on  and on and on for me the knight rider  should not be a movie  if you do a movie it should just be  something that starts a new franchise  it should be something that goes  straight to amazon or netflix james one  producing this wants to make a cinematic  movie but  it 